Smart contract tests are located in `test/flashLoan.test.js` and run using `npm test` (which executes `truffle test`). 

Tests utilize Truffle's testing environment and `@openzeppelin/test-helpers`. 

Crucially, testing the core `requestFlashLoan` functionality requires running against a Sepolia fork. This is configured as the `development_fork` network in `truffle-config.js` and typically needs to be started manually (e.g., `ganache --fork <SEPOLIA_RPC_URL>`). Tests anticipate potential arbitrage failures on the fork due to unpredictable market conditions.
